{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/news/uk-spends-over-400-million-on-long-range-weapons-as-cooperation-scales-up-with-european-allies","content_id":"8ae5eb48-a92f-4300-ac89-904e314ec84f","description":"UK will spend over £400 million this financial year on hypersonic and long-range weapons including joint projects with France, Germany, and Italy.","details":{"attachments":[],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>The UK is scaling up cooperation with key European allies to develop new long-range precision and hypersonic weapons, with spending on projects set to exceed £400 million this financial year.</p>\n\n<p>Britain is progressing the Stratus joint missile programme with France and Italy – leading the work to develop a next generation stealth replacement to the Storm Shadow missile.</p>\n\n<p>Stratus, which is developing both stealth and high-speed missile variants, already sustains over 1,300 high-skilled jobs in the UK. The new missiles will be able to defeat high-value targets, destroy enemy ships, and suppress enemy air defences.</p>\n\n<p>At the same time, Britian’s new long-range weapon programme with Germany is progressing rapidly with a new joint study phase about to begin, accelerating both future stealth and hypersonic weapons. This follows the landmark UK-Germany Trinity House Agreement signed within the first months of this Government in 2024.</p>\n\n<p>The new system – known as Deep Precision Strike – will have a range of over 2,000 km and be among the most advanced systems ever designed by the UK, coming into service in the 2030s. Long-range weapons are crucial to protecting the UK and our allies and boosting NATO deterrence.</p>\n\n<p>The government has committed to the largest sustained increase in defence spending since the end of the Cold War – hitting 2.6% of GDP from 2027 – to ensure that Britain and our allies are safe.</p>\n\n<h3 id=\"defence-secretary-john-healey-mp-said\">Defence Secretary John Healey MP said:</h3>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p>To meet this new era of rising threats, we need hard power, strong alliances and sure diplomacy.</p>\n\n  <p>We can see from the war in Ukraine the decisive impact of long-range precision weapons, so the UK is stepping up, investing more than £400 million for long-range and hypersonic weapons this year.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"last-child\">Alongside Germany, France and Italy, we will deliver the cutting-edge weapons that will keep the UK and NATO safe, boost deterrence, and build a new deal for European security.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<p>Hypersonic weapons investment this year also includes funding for developing critical technologies, ground and flight testing, as well as significant funding for academic skills and training including funding post-graduate study.</p>\n\n<p>The Defence Secretary is expected to discuss these projects and deepening industrial cooperation during crucial meetings with European and international allies at the Munich Security Conference.</p>\n\n<p>This ramped up missile cooperation by European allies comes as Russia’s aggression in Ukraine continues. In early February, UK Defence Intelligence confirmed that Russia conducted a major multi-axis and multi-weapon strike on Ukraine, using long range bombers, hypersonic missiles, over 60 ballistic and cruise missiles, and 450 one-way attack drones.</p>\n\n<p>The Defence Secretary is expected to talk to allies during a series of bilateral meetings at the Munich Security Conference about boosting support for Ukraine, defending Europe against growing Russian threats,  and enhancing industrial partnerships with key allies and partners.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-02-13T13:00:01Z"}],"emphasised_organisations":["d994e55c-48c9-4795-b872-58d8ec98af12"],"images":[{"caption":null,"content_type":"image/jpeg","sources":{"s216":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46e90e0731ae2a1415/s216_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s300":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d468fa8f5346732690e/s300_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s465":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d468fa8f53468995326/s465_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s630":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46e90e0731a983a846/s630_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s712":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46e90e0731a4dcff75/s712_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s960":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46d3bf7f618eda94d2/s960_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg"},"type":"lead"}],"political":true},"document_type":"press_release","first_published_at":"2026-02-13T13:00:01+00:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/news/uk-spends-over-400-million-on-long-range-weapons-as-cooperation-scales-up-with-european-allies","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/news/uk-spends-over-400-million-on-long-range-weapons-as-cooperation-scales-up-with-european-allies","base_path":"/government/news/uk-spends-over-400-million-on-long-range-weapons-as-cooperation-scales-up-with-european-allies","content_id":"8ae5eb48-a92f-4300-ac89-904e314ec84f","document_type":"press_release","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-02-13T13:00:01Z","schema_name":"news_article","title":"UK spends over £400 million on long-range weapons as cooperation scales up with European allies","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/news/uk-spends-over-400-million-on-long-range-weapons-as-cooperation-scales-up-with-european-allies","withdrawn":false}],"emphasised_organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D17","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","base_path":"/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","content_id":"d994e55c-48c9-4795-b872-58d8ec98af12","details":{"acronym":"MOD","brand":"ministry-of-defence","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46d3bf7f618eda94d2/s960_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d468fa8f5346732690e/s300_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"mod","formatted_title":"Ministry<br/>of Defence"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Ministry of Defence","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","withdrawn":false}],"government":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","base_path":"/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","content_id":"9dbff654-cdeb-4ebe-9a12-cd4cc20a033e","details":{"current":false,"ended_on":"2026-07-20T00:00:00+00:00","started_on":"2024-07-05T00:00:00+00:00"},"document_type":"government","links":{},"locale":"en","title":"2024 to 2026 Starmer Labour government","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/2024-starmer-labour-government"}],"organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D17","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","base_path":"/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","content_id":"d994e55c-48c9-4795-b872-58d8ec98af12","details":{"acronym":"MOD","brand":"ministry-of-defence","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46d3bf7f618eda94d2/s960_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d468fa8f5346732690e/s300_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"mod","formatted_title":"Ministry<br/>of Defence"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Ministry of Defence","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","withdrawn":false}],"people":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/people/john-healey","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/people/john-healey","base_path":"/government/people/john-healey","content_id":"6e000fab-7c45-479a-8362-53a971f31f28","document_type":"person","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-20T17:50:11Z","schema_name":"person","title":"The Rt Hon John Healey MP","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/people/john-healey","withdrawn":false}],"primary_publishing_organisation":[{"analytics_identifier":"D17","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","base_path":"/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","content_id":"d994e55c-48c9-4795-b872-58d8ec98af12","details":{"acronym":"MOD","brand":"ministry-of-defence","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46d3bf7f618eda94d2/s960_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d468fa8f5346732690e/s300_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"mod","formatted_title":"Ministry<br/>of Defence"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Ministry of Defence","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","withdrawn":false}],"roles":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/ministers/secretary-of-state-for-defence","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/ministers/secretary-of-state-for-defence","base_path":"/government/ministers/secretary-of-state-for-defence","content_id":"845e5e80-c0f1-11e4-8223-005056011aef","details":{"body":"<p>The Secretary of State for Defence has overall responsibility for the business of the department.</p>\n\n<p>Responsibilities include:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Strategic policy and operational oversight including as a member of the National Security Council</li>\n  <li>Nuclear deterrent (CASD) and operations policy and enterprise</li>\n  <li>Strategic overview of the Strategic Defence Review Implementation and Defence Investment Plan</li>\n  <li>Defence budget</li>\n  <li>Euro-Atlantic strategy and planning</li>\n  <li>Defence strategy, planning, programme, and resource allocation</li>\n  <li>Relationships with strategic international partners: US, France, Germany, Australia, Ukraine</li>\n  <li>One Defence Reform Programme</li>\n  <li>Oversight of Veterans</li>\n  <li>Service Personnel deaths on duty and letters of condolence</li>\n  <li>Strategic multilateral programmes – AUKUS and GCAP</li>\n  <li>Regulatory functions</li>\n  <li>Support on Afghan Inquiry</li>\n</ul>\n","role_payment_type":null,"seniority":11,"whip_organisation":{}},"document_type":"ministerial_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-08-14T12:39:26Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Secretary of State for Defence","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/secretary-of-state-for-defence","withdrawn":false}],"taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/defence/working-armed-forces","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/defence/working-armed-forces","base_path":"/defence/working-armed-forces","content_id":"8ff8cf05-a6e6-4757-a896-4fabd9f3229a","details":{"internal_name":"Armed forces [M] (level 2, defence theme)","notes_for_editors":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":false},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"parent_taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/defence-and-armed-forces","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/defence-and-armed-forces","base_path":"/defence-and-armed-forces","content_id":"e491505c-77ae-45b2-84be-8c94b94f6a2b","description":"","details":{"internal_name":"Defence and armed forces","notes_for_editors":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":true},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"root_taxon":[{"api_path":"/api/content/","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/","base_path":"/","content_id":"f3bbdec2-0e62-4520-a7fd-6ffd5d36e03a","document_type":"homepage","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-02-18T13:00:23Z","schema_name":"homepage","title":"GOV.UK homepage","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2018-09-16T20:34:16Z","schema_name":"taxon","title":"Defence and armed forces","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/defence-and-armed-forces","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2018-09-05T16:16:52Z","schema_name":"taxon","title":"Armed forces","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/defence/working-armed-forces","withdrawn":false}]},"locale":"en","phase":"live","public_updated_at":"2026-02-13T13:00:01+00:00","publishing_app":"whitehall","publishing_request_id":"21-1773658115.790-10.13.22.163-2742","publishing_scheduled_at":"2026-02-13T13:00:00+00:00","rendering_app":"frontend","scheduled_publishing_delay_seconds":2,"schema_name":"news_article","title":"UK spends over £400 million on long-range weapons as cooperation scales up with European allies","updated_at":"2026-08-14T17:36:06+01:00","withdrawn_notice":{}}